# tools/master-remove.list: packages of the card that an image for other people does without.
# The compressed image must stay under 2 GiB (one file of a GitHub release). The card is the owner's working system
# and carries what he installed to bring the board up, and Fedora's image carries what a general-purpose desktop
# brings: 13 GiB together. tools/master-image.sh removes the groups below with dnf, inside the image, one transaction
# per line: "<what it is>|<package names or globs>". Whatever is here can be installed again with dnf.
# A group whose removal would take out any package the image is about (the desktop, the GPU stack, the a7a packages,
# networking, Firefox, dnf itself: the GUARD list in master-image.sh) stops the build instead of being removed;
# dependencies nothing else needs go with their group (dnf's clean_requirements_on_remove).
# 2026-11-16, measured on a copy: 13.0 GiB -> 7.4 GiB, 2128 MiB as .xz before the last two lines and the SDK's
# .git directory (630 MiB compressed, half of it history) were dealt with.

# -- what the owner installed to bring the board up
the game and its data|supertuxkart supertuxkart-data
compilers and build tools|llvm-static llvm llvm-devel clang* gcc gcc-c++ cpp cmake compiler-rt gdb strace perf apitrace meson ninja-build libstdc++-devel glibc-devel kernel-headers vulkan-headers
development files|*-devel *-static
benchmarks and test tools (glmark2 stays: a7a-clock soak runs it)|sysbench stress-ng fio memtester iperf3 vkmark weston
cloud client libraries|python3-botocore python3-boto3 python3-s3transfer
containers|podman buildah skopeo

# -- what Fedora's image brings and this board has no use for
U-Boot images for other boards|uboot-images-armv8
firmware of other hardware|qcom-firmware qcom-wwan-firmware nvidia-gpu-firmware amd-gpu-firmware intel-gpu-firmware iwlwifi-*-firmware iwlegacy-firmware bcm2*-firmware tiwilink-firmware intel-audio-firmware cirrus-audio-firmware nxpwireless-firmware libertas-firmware amd-ucode-firmware
Fedora's own kernel (this board boots the a7a kernels)|kernel kernel-core kernel-modules kernel-modules-core
the SELinux troubleshooter (the a7a kernels run without SELinux: its applet failed at every login, 2026-11-17)|setroubleshoot setroubleshoot-server setroubleshoot-plugins

# -- what a desktop can do without until somebody wants it back
geodata grids|proj-data-?? proj-data-eur
LibreOffice and Java|libreoffice* java-*-openjdk*
extra wallpapers|plasma-workspace-wallpapers
browser language packs|firefox-langpacks
KDE mail and calendar (PIM) with its database|akonadi* kmail korganizer kaddressbook kontact mariadb*
